 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-002\",\n \"clauses\": {\"present_data\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"Make a picture graph to show: {data_str}. Draw one {symbol} for each item.\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 is a presenting task: it asks the learner to make a picture graph from the data in data_str, which is nested F09 text drawn from the _THEMES row. Its symbol slot reads the same row (one_row_per_problem true), so the drawing key matches the problem's categories.\"},\n  \"pictograph\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"Complete the picture graph for {data_str}. Draw one {symbol} for each item.\", \"reasoning\": \"F05 names the representation as a picture graph and asks the learner to draw one symbol per item, which is the pictograph form. F01 supplies the word 'pictograph' only in hints via F04, and the vocabulary gate prints it for this lc.\"},\n  \"without_scale\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F07\", \"template\": \"Make a picture graph to show: {data_str}. Draw one {symbol} for each item.\", \"reasoning\": \"The one-symbol-per-item rule in F07 gives a graph with no scale: each picture stands for one item and no scale value is printed or required. The only declared variant is scale_type no_scale, and no template prints a scale. The F03 hint 'Each picture stands for 1 item.' supports the same property.\"}},\n \"failing_families\": [],\n \"failing_templates\": [],\n \"overall\": \"PASS\",\n \"reasoning\": \"Vocabulary: F01 prints only 'pictograph' (requires_vocab pictograph, words_left_out 1), which is in this lc's introduces_vocab. No printed family uses a NOT_YET_KNOWN term. The words 'picture graph', 'survey', 'category' and 'item' appear in F02, F05 to F08 and are not in NOT_YET_KNOWN. Numbers: the counts are 1 to 5 under F09 v2 (one of the generator's own choices, members 1 to 5), which fits the no-commas number format. Symbols: _THEMES symbol fields are emoji drawn from one row per problem (one_row_per_problem true), so the key matches the row's categories. Observed weaknesses that are not wrong statements: F05 and F06 say 'picture graph' where no graph is shown; the symbol for some rows (for example the paw-print symbol for the animals row, or the book symbol for the days row) is a loose fit for its categories; and F09 prints a single category and count per problem, so the question shows one data point. None makes a statement false or unreadable for a grade 1 quarter 3 learner, so the overall verdict is PASS.\"}",
